so the first trailer is out for the tomb  raider movie starring Alicia vikander  and I had a few thoughts that I wanted  to put out there I didn't think it was  gonna have any I hadn't planned to do a  video when the trailer came out but when  I did actually see the thing I'm like I  think I gotta talk this one out a little  bit so first of all for context I don't  have a particularly heavy investment in  the Tomb Raider games I played them yeah  I've played them a little bit off and on  across the series never been a huge fan  but I've always kind of followed it to a  certain extent I mean I'm like that with  gaming in general there's lots of sort  of franchises and stuff that I follow  what's going on  in them because I find that stuff  interesting even though I don't play a  lot of games anymore but I do have a  very strong soft spot for the previous  Lara Croft film starring Angelina Jolie  and I say that knowing they're not  actually all that good but I enjoy them  I actually own both of them and I kind  of set them aside along with the first  Mortal Kombat film in that look I know  it's not great but as far as video game  movies go this is pretty decent and my  feeling about those previous films is  that they in terms of the action the  styling they're very much of the era  they were made and late 90s early 2000s  excepting the matrix wasn't actually a  great period for action movies in a lot  of ways once the matrix hit things got  better again but these ones that you can  still sort of feel the 90s miss them  even though they are actually early  2000s movies but it's buoyed by Angelina  Jolie's performance because I think  she's magnetic and fun and just a  wonderful to watch in the part so my  thoughts on this trailer kept going back  and forth because I'd seen the images  early on you know sort of the the  initial images of her with a bow looking  all dirty I saw that one  oh okay they're going new Lara Croft  they're going to reboot version this is  very 