 although if you do it  correctly whatever the extra element is  could be a nice surprise so I don't envy  the marketers trying to sell this movie  but there's just something that isn't  gelling for me as we're jumping between  you know her you know being in a very  dire situation like  this glyph and hitting this this tree on  the way down and the impact it hits hard  and feels like it hurts like odd you  know that doesn't feel like fun action  damage that felt like a hard impactful  hit and then at the end show her with  the guns that Lara that the angelina  jolie version was known for and being oh  I'll take two and like that those are  mixing for me and I don't know if I'm  alone in this opinion I haven't bothered  to check what reactions to this trailer  like before I record this cuz I want my  opinion to be my own opinion and not a  response to what everyone else is saying  so I might be the only one with this  issue I fully accept that that is a  distinct possibility but yeah there's  something about trying to marry the dark  gritty and the fun action elements of  this franchise that at least as far as  the trailer is presenting it the two  aren't blending well now I I will keep  an eye out for a next trailer I've said  in the past that when when I see a  trailer that sells me on a movie I'm  like I'm definitely gonna see that I  basically stop watching future trailers  because I don't want to get spoiled this  one I'm really on the fence about so I  will keep an eye out for future trailers  and see if they can sort of give me a  better sense of what the final product  is going to be I just worry that this  sort of schizophrenic nature of these  elements is just gonna just turn some  people off and not turn them off as like  I'm not gonna go see that but just fail  to sell it hard enough that people will  go out of their way it's more of a oh  maybe if I'm not doing anything that  weekend and that kind of response is  more or less where something like prince 